From 22a86e19f47e0468aa7ed834ec372d956c1387ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] db: migrate the daemon database wrapper to MDBX

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add the libmdbx CDBWrapper and Chronik storage backend with automatic migration
from legacy LevelDB and RocksDB databases.

Original-Commit: be9d70e3f86dd845b57ba15fa9568529957247e6
Original-Patch: ecash/004
Split-Concern: daemon-db

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Declare the optional CCoinsView prefetch hint at its first MDBX-era caller. The default is intentionally a no-op; concrete readahead overrides remain in original ecash/026. No validation decision or storage semantics change.

Fixture-Repair: Fold f6d2066dcaf7bad367c622a2bde4f443f4641001 into
this first CDBWrapper MDBX owner. feature_init now targets mdbx.dat,
requires nonempty file matches, asserts strict missing/corrupt/open errors,
and retains all seven corruption rounds including all three metadata replicas.
The previous LevelDB glob matched no files and expected-init-error waited600s.
On unchanged shared45fc417 binaries, the repaired fixture passed20 startup
interruptions,4 deletion refusals and7 corruption refusals. This is test-only
shared evidence; native-header corruption adaptation and final native run
are separate. No production storage/recovery semantics change.
